6 so far: 11 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","change":"Helena's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","rain":"Helena has gotten drier"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 51\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>51\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 45\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1999, 2025). The low of <strong>27\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","p_rec":"If Helena's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Helena has set <strong class=\"sig\">18 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 67 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">150 record highs</strong>, far more than the 67 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (59). Helena's all-time high is 105\u00b0F, on August 24, 1969.","t_chg":"Helena's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","p_chg":"Across 145 complete years: Helena's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.06\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.14 to +0.02) that includes zero. Helena's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.39\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.32 to +0.46), about +5.7\u00b0F since 1881. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.99\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.54 to +1.45) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 3 months fell. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Helena has gotten drier","p_rain":"Helena's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.16 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.28 to \u22120.04), about \u22122.3 inches since 1882. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 11.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1975 (20.94 in); the driest, 1973 (6.26 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}